{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CfeW41htQdKoxBULwYxyo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe membership-level computation is now duplicated verbatim across two units. `OwnerMapper.toMembershipLevel(Owner)` and `ClinicServiceImpl.computeMembershipLevel(Owner)` contain byte-for-byte identical logic (start at 1, +1 for email, +1 for `namesakeCount == 0`, cap at 3) *and* an identical Javadoc paragraph. Before this change the audit line computed nothing, so the diff introduced the second copy — this is new duplication, not pre-existing.\n\nThe business rule for deriving a level now has two owners that must be kept in sync. The spec even flags that level 4 (tenure) is a future addition; when that lands, a maintainer has to remember to edit both places, and they can silently drift.\n\nConcrete options to consolidate into a single home:\n\n- **Preferred — put it on the domain model.** The level is derived purely from the `Owner`'s own fields (`email`, `namesakeCount`), so a derived accessor on `Owner` (e.g. `getMembershipLevel()`) is the natural single source. Both the mapper's `@Mapping` and the audit line then read the same method, and the Javadoc lives once.\n- **Alternatively**, have `ClinicServiceImpl` reuse the mapper. If `OwnerMapper` is already a Spring bean, inject it and call `toMembershipLevel(owner)` from the audit path instead of reimplementing it, rather than maintaining a private copy.\n\nEither way, the goal is one definition of the rule. The rest of the change (field rename in the mapper/DTO mapping, the audit line now recording `membershipLevel`, and the OpenAI/OpenAPI schema switch to a bounded `integer` with matching description/example) is coherent and in the right place."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8177,"cache_read_input_tokens":11894,"cache_cr